  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Communications in advocacy work to resolve environmental conflicts</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project seeks to address the socio-environmental conflicts that are a crucial feature of the development debate life in Peru today through strengthening the capacity of local radio stations (mainly Church-run) and community leaders to intervene more effectively in these debates.  It will provide these groups with better information on the environmental and social issues involved (including climate change and indigenous rights) and seek to improve their communications and advocacy techniques.

The project will operate in four of Peru&#x2019;s macro-regions, North-East (based in Cajamarca), East (based in Iquitos, the Amazon), Central Highlands (based in Huancayo), Southern Andes (based in Sicuani).  CAFOD&#x2019;s main contribution is likely to be via the Southern Andes, which is our priority region in Peru.</narrative>
  </description>
